---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
const title = 'Do Solar Panels Work on Cloudy Days? Thailand Monsoon Guide';
const description = "Solar panels still generate 10–25% output on cloudy days. Learn how modern panels perform during Thailand's monsoon season and why weather is not a dealbreaker.";
---
<Layout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  ogType="article"
  jsonLd={{
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "Article",
    "headline": title,
    "description": description,
    "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "JJ Com Solar Cell" },
    "publisher": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "JJ Com Solar Cell" },
    "datePublished": "2024-06-01",
    "mainEntityOfPage": { "@type": "WebPage", "@id": "https://www.kohchangsolarcell.com/guides/solar-panels-cloudy-days/" }
  }}
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="text-sm text-gray-500 mb-6">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-solar-green">Home</a> / <span>Guides</span> / <span>Cloudy Day Performance</span>
    </nav>

    <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-4">Do Solar Panels Work on Cloudy Days? A Thailand Monsoon Guide</h1>
    <p class="text-gray-600 mb-8">
      Worried about the rainy season? Modern solar technology captures diffuse light and continues generating power 
      even during overcast skies. Here's what to expect in Thailand.
    </p>

    <div class="bg-solar-green/5 rounded-xl p-6 mb-8">
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 text-center">
        <div>
          <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-solar-green">10–25%</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">of rated output on cloudy days</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-solar-green">60–80%</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">of rated output on partly cloudy days</div>
        </div>
        <div>
          <div class="text-3xl font-bold text-solar-green">90–100%</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">on bright sunny days</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">How Solar Panels Handle Cloud Cover</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        Solar panels don't need direct sunlight to work. They absorb both <strong>direct</strong> and <strong>diffuse</strong> light. 
        When clouds block the sun, scattered (diffuse) light still reaches the panels from all directions. Modern monocrystalline panels 
        are especially efficient at capturing this indirect light.
      </p>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-100">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Direct Light</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Bright sun, clear skies — maximum output. Panels reach full rated capacity.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm border border-gray-100">
          <h3 class="font-bold mb-2">Diffuse Light</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">Cloudy/overcast — reduced but steady output. Modern panels still capture significant energy from scattered light.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Thailand Monsoon Season Output</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        Thailand's rainy season runs roughly <strong>May–October</strong>. While daily output drops, it does not stop. 
        Here's what a typical 5 kW system produces:
      </p>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto">
        <table class="w-full text-sm border-collapse">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50">
              <th class="p-3 text-left border">Weather Condition</th>
              <th class="p-3 text-center border">Daily Output (5 kW)</th>
              <th class="p-3 text-center border">% of Rated Capacity</th>
              <th class="p-3 text-center border">Typical Days/Month</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><td class="p-3 border">Bright sun, no clouds</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">25–30 kWh</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">100%</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">10–15 (dry season)</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="p-3 border">Partly cloudy</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">18–22 kWh</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">70–80%</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">8–12</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="p-3 border">Overcast/light rain</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">8–12 kWh</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">30–45%</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">3–6</td></tr>
            <tr class="bg-gray-50"><td class="p-3 border">Heavy rain/storms</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">3–6 kWh</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">10–20%</td><td class="p-3 border text-center">2–4</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Why Rainy Season Is Not a Dealbreaker</h2>
      <ul class="space-y-3">
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-solar-green">✓</span> <span><strong>Cooler temperatures improve efficiency:</strong> Panels actually work better in cooler weather. A 25°C day with clouds can outperform a 40°C sunny day.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-solar-green">✓</span> <span><strong>Rain cleans panels naturally:</strong> Dust and dirt wash away, improving output once the sun returns.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-solar-green">✓</span> <span><strong>Annual average matters:</strong> A solar system is sized based on yearly production, not worst-case days. Thailand's long dry season compensates.</span></li>
        <li class="flex items-start gap-2"><span class="text-solar-green">✓</span> <span><strong>Battery storage smooths supply:</strong> Store excess dry-season energy for rainy days. See our <a href="/guides/solar-system-sizing-calculator/" class="text-solar-green underline">sizing guide</a> for battery recommendations.</span></li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Panel Durability in Tropical Weather</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        Quality solar panels are engineered to withstand Thailand's harsh conditions — heavy rain, high humidity, UV exposure, and salt air near coastal areas. 
        All panels we install carry IEC 61215 certification for tropical climate endurance.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-slate-50 to-blue-50 rounded-xl p-8 mb-12">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Related Guides</h2>
      <div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
        <a href="/guides/solar-sunlight-hours/" class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow border border-gray-100">
          <div class="font-bold">Sunlight Hours in Thailand</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Monthly peak sun data by region</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/guides/solar-system-sizing-calculator/" class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow border border-gray-100">
          <div class="font-bold">System Sizing Calculator</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Size your system for year-round production</div>
        </a>
        <a href="/guides/solar-panel-maintenance/" class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg shadow-sm hover:shadow-md transition-shadow border border-gray-100">
          <div class="font-bold">Maintenance & Cleaning Guide</div>
          <div class="text-sm text-gray-600">Post-monsoon cleaning tips</div>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <div class="bg-solar-green text-white rounded-xl p-8 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-2">Don't Let Weather Worry You</h2>
      <p class="mb-6">Our systems are designed for Thailand's climate. Get a free assessment and see your estimated year-round savings.</p>
      <a href="/#contact" class="inline-block bg-white text-solar-green font-semibold px-8 py-3 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-100 transition-colors">
        Get a Free Assessment
      </a>
      <p class="text-sm mt-4 opacity-80">
        Ask about our <a href="/" class="underline">complete solar system installation</a> with battery backup.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Layout>
